  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "Built Coin Dash in src/sim.ts (pure, seeded, deterministic simulation) and src/main.ts (Aura3D rendering, input, DOM HUD, fixed-step loop). Typecheck passes. I could not run `vite build` or open the game in a browser, so the rendering is unverified.\n\n- **Gameplay:** A sphere player moves on a plane arena with arrow keys or WASD. There are 10 coins. Collecting one gives +1 score and respawns that coin elsewhere using a seeded RNG, which is re-seeded on each restart. The round lasts 30s: it becomes `won` immediately at score 15 and `lost` at 30s otherwise.\n- **Controls:** `P` toggles pause, which freezes the simulation. `R` restarts with score 0, time 0 and status `playing`.\n- **Fixed timestep:** The rAF loop uses an accumulator with a 1/60 step, so the simulation does not depend on display refresh.\n- **HUD:** DOM elements `#score`, `#time` (remaining seconds) and `#status` sit outside the canvas.\n- **Test hooks:** `window.__EVAL__ = { state, step }` is set up. `step(n)` runs n fixed steps immediately with the current input and does nothing while paused or after the round ends. `__EVAL_READY__` is set after the renderer is ready and the first frame has run, or after a 5s fallback.\n- **Rendering and resilience:** Aura3D draws into the existing `#app` canvas, using primitives for the player, coins, floor and walls. If renderer setup throws, the error is logged and the simulation and HUD still work.",
